{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTEwMTA=","is_bot":false,"login":"mjcuva","name":"Marc Cuva"},"body":"## Why\n\nOur second enterprise customer ran `npx restless init` in their docs repo rather than their API repo (discussed in today's 14 at 4). The repo had a `package.json` and a little JS, so the stack check treated it as a Node repo, and the coding-agent playbook told the agent to \"find the API yourself\" in a repo with no API.\n\n## What changes\n\n**Deterministic layer** (`lib/detect-stack.js`): `detectStack` now reports `likelyDocs` and `docsEvidence`. The verdict needs positive docs evidence (a generator dependency such as Docusaurus, VitePress, Nextra, Starlight, Mintlify or rdme; a generator config file; or a Markdown-heavy tree) **and** zero server evidence of any kind: no server dependency, no foreign-language manifest, no route or server marker in source. Astro and Next.js count as server deps, so a static-site generator that serves endpoints is never stopped. It is not a count of JavaScript files.\n\n**Coding-agent path** (`bin/restless.js`): on `likelyDocs` the playbook is replaced by a short stop that cites the evidence, says Restless wires into the server code, tells the agent to ask the user where the API lives, and prints the existing `RESTLESS_SKIP_STACK_CHECK=1` escape hatch. For repos the check cannot call, the playbook's \"found no framework\" section (`lib/agent-plan.js`) now tells the agent to confirm the repo holds a server before starting and to stop rather than invent an API.\n\n**Interactive path** (`steps/generate-oas.js`): the same message becomes a yes/no, \"Scan it for an API anyway?\", defaulting to no. Declining marks the run unfinished so the help offer still fires. The endpoint-detection prompt (`prompts/detect-endpoints.md`) also returns a `repoKind`, so an empty result in a docs site or frontend reads \"This looks like a documentation site\" instead of \"We couldn't find any APIs\".\n\nREADME gets a paragraph under the stack-check section.\n\n## Tests\n\n17 new tests: the Docusaurus shape, a nested `docs/` site, a Markdown-heavy tree with a bare `package.json`, and the non-cases (docs beside Express, docs beside FastAPI, Next.js and Astro sites, a bare `node:http` preview server, a library with a README and changelog). Full suite: 1314 passing.\n\nSmoke-tested the real binary in a fake Docusaurus repo under a coding agent, with and without the escape hatch. The self-drive path waits on a keypress at the welcome screen, so its copy is unit-tested only; worth one manual run in a docs repo before release.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":[{"path":"README.md","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"bin/restless.js","additions":13,"deletions":6,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"lib/agent-plan.js","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"lib/detect-stack.js","additions":134,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"prompts/detect-endpoints.md","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"steps/generate-oas.js","additions":76,"deletions":7,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tests/agent-plan.test.js","additions":19,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tests/detect-stack.test.js","additions":129,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"tests/generate-oas-no-api.test.js","additions":38,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"}],"headRefName":"granola-docs-issue-fix-0c65e3da","state":"OPEN","title":"Stop `init` in a docs repo instead of hunting for an API in it"}
